With my trusty Ipaq I descend into the depths of the New York mass transit 
system every day... every once in a while a YAAP emerges.

Chris was another random start, a Orcish Ranger who gave up the bow as soon 
as a decent stack of daggers presented itself.  Daggers would be the only 
weapon I would use after an early find of a sliver dagger.  Geno and 
Polyless would be the only tracked conducts, but I was determined to go 
un-crowned, without any artifact gifts and without ever reading a spellbook. 
Not that i'd be avoiding prayer.  (not until the late/endgame with Mars 
angry.)

Minetown had two magic lamps, so I blessed one for GDSM, I got it at +2. 
The quest wasn't diffucult, just annoying.  That damn spiral.

I hit one bonesfile, a pretty statue of a post-quest knight who was still 
reaching for the cockatrice corpse that petrified him.  I had found a HooA, 
so I levelported back to my stash and lost 9 points of protection (d'oh!) in 
return for the Magic Mirror of Merlin.  I'd go without the protection for 
the rest of the game.

I had a nice stack of +6 orcish daggers until Orcustown when a monster 
picked them up and then got a whiff of black dragon breath, taking them all 
away (Ouch)  I did enchant up a stack of elven daggers later but they got 
less use.

I ended up using up my "oLS in a summoning storm during rodney's first 
re-appearence in the main dungeon, I discovered that I couldn't get into my 
bag for a !oFH, which is why it's better to weild an artifact weapon, 
Wearing a cursed SoR, Silver Dagger, and =oLevitation can be a real pain.  I 
managed to get Mars angry by praying too soon after killing some annoying 
gremlins, so I ended up using a sink to lose the ring and then dipping my 
dagger into fountains until I got it uncursed.

Rodney re-appeared several times before that happened and he ended up with 
quite an inventory before I got away.  In addition to the AoY, he got all 
three invocation artifacts.  He would have gotten the longbow too if I 
hadn't stashed it right after completing the quest.  A good thing he doesn't 
steal other classes quest artifacts, or I might have had a real problem 
killing him. As it stood, after getting back into my bag and re-charging 
Orcus' toy I made short work of him for the eleventh time and ran for the 
planes where the last thing Rodney saw in the entire game was labeled 
Orcus'.

The planes were not too diffucult I used !oConfusion and ?oGD to find the 
portals, using /oT on the air elementals to avoid too much battering on air, 
and dashed across fire.  The wait on water wasn't bad, and I decided to head 
right on astral, using the last charge on Orcus' wand on Pesty and digging 
out another /oD.  The high priest of Mars gave me two bits and I pulled out 
my organic magic whistle to bring in my gaurdian angel.

